iao:0000144 iao:0000111 "conclusion textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 "that fucoidan has a small statistically significant effect on AT3 level but no useful clinical effect as in-vivo anticoagulant, a paraphrase of part of the last paragraph of the discussion section of the paper 'Pilot clinical study to evaluate the anticoagulant activity of fucoidan', by Lowenthal et. al.PMID:19696660"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity that expresses the results of reasoning about a problem, for instance as typically found towards the end of scientific papers."@en;
            iao:0000116 "2009/09/28 Alan Ruttenberg. Fucoidan-use-case"@en,
                        "2009/10/23 Alan Ruttenberg: We need to work on the definition still"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            iao:0000412 pobo:iao.owl;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Conclusion Textual Entity";
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030.
iao:0000221 iao:0000115 """m is a quality measurement of q at t when
q is a quality 
there is a measurement process p that has specified output m, a measurement datum, that is about q"""@en;
            iao:0000116 """This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details."""@en,
                        """From the second IAO workshop [Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009: not completely current, though bringing in comparison is probably important]

This one is the one we are struggling with at the moment. The issue is what a measurement measures. On the one hand saying that it measures the quality would include it \"measuring\" the bearer = referring to the bearer in the measurement. However this makes comparisons of two different things not possible. On the other hand not having it inhere in the bearer, on the face of it, breaks the audit trail.

Werner suggests a solution based on \"Magnitudes\" a proposal for which we are awaiting details.
--
From the second IAO workshop, various comments, [commented on by Alan Ruttenberg 8/6/2009]

unit of measure is a quality, e.g. the length of a ruler.

[We decided to hedge on what units of measure are, instead talking about measurement unit labels, which are the information content entities that are about whatever measurement units are. For IAO we need that information entity in any case. See the term measurement unit label]

[Some struggling with the various subflavors of is_about. We subsequently removed the relation represents, and describes until and only when we have a better theory]

a represents b means either a denotes b or a describes

describe:
a describes b means a is about b and a allows an inference of at least one quality of b

We have had a long discussion about denotes versus describes."""@en,
                        """From the second meeting on IAO:

An attempt at defining assay using Barry's \"reliability\" wording

assay:
process and has_input some material entity
and has_output some information content entity 
and which is such that instances of this process type reliably generate 
outputs that describes the input."""@en,
                        """From the second IAO workshop: An attempt at tieing the quality to the measurement datum more carefully.

a is a magnitude means a is a determinate quality particular inhering in some bearer b existing at a time t that can be represented/denoted by an information content entity e that has parts denoting a unit of measure, a number, and b. The unit of measure is an instance of the determinable quality."""@en,
                        "8/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg: The strategy is to be rather specific with this relationship. There are other kinds of measurements that are not of qualities, such as those that measure time. We will add these as separate properties for the moment and see about generalizing later"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:domain iao:0000109;
            rdfs:label "is quality measurement of";
            rdfs:range pobo:BFO_0000019;
            rdfs:subPropertyOf iao:0000136.
iao:0000227 rdfs:label "terms merged".
iao:0000231 a owl:AnnotationProperty.
iao:0000232 a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "curator note".
iao:0000300 iao:0000111 "textual entity"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Words, sentences, paragraphs, and the written (non-figure) parts of publications are all textual entities"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A textual entity is a part of a manifestation (FRBR sense), a generically dependent continuant whose concretizations are patterns of glyphs intended to be interpreted as words, formulas, etc."@en;
            iao:0000116 "AR, (IAO call 2009-09-01): a document as a whole is not typically a textual entity, because it has pictures in it - rather there are parts of it that are textual entities. Examples: The title, paragraph 2 sentence 7, etc."@en,
                        "MC, 2009-09-14 (following IAO call 2009-09-01): textual entities live at the FRBR (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_Requirements_for_Bibliographic_Records) manifestation level. Everything is significant: line break, pdf and html versions of same document are different textual entities."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Lawrence Hunter"@en;
            iao:0000118 "text"@en;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Textual Entity";
            rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030.
iao:0000412 a owl:AnnotationProperty;
            rdfs:label "imported from".
iao:0000417 iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "inverse of the relation of is quality measurement of"@en;
            iao:0000116 "2009/10/19 Alan Ruttenberg. Named 'junk' relation useful in restrictions, but not a real instance relationship"@en;
            iao:0000117 "Person:Alan Ruttenberg"@en;
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:label "is quality measured as";
            owl:inverseOf iao:0000221.
obi:0000011 iao:0000111 "planned process"@en,
                        "planned process";
            iao:0000112 "Injecting mice with a vaccine in order to test its efficacy";
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "A processual entity that realizes a plan which is the concretization of a plan specification."@en;
            iao:0000116 "'Plan' includes a future direction sense. That can be problematic if plans are changed during their execution. There are however implicit contingencies for protocols that an agent has in his mind that can be considered part of the plan, even if the agent didn't have them in mind before. Therefore, a planned process can diverge from what the agent would have said the plan was before executing it, by adjusting to problems encountered during execution (e.g. choosing another reagent with equivalent properties, if the originally planned one has run out.)";
            iao:0000117 "Bjoern Peters";
            iao:0000119 "branch derived";
            iao:0000412 pobo:obi.owl;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Planned Process";
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000015.
obi:0000017 iao:0000111 "regulatory role"@en;
            iao:0000112 "Regulatory agency, Ethics committee, Approval letter; example:  Browse these EPA Regulatory Role subtopics  http://www.epa.gov/ebtpages/enviregulatoryrole.html  Feb 29, 2008"@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000120;
            iao:0000115 "a role which inheres in material entities and is realized in the processes of making, enforcing or being defined by legislation or orders issued by a governmental body."@en;
            iao:0000117 "GROUP:  Role branch"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI, CDISC"@en;
            iao:0000412 pobo:obi.owl;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Regulatory Role";
            rdfs:subClassOf pobo:BFO_0000023.
obi:0000272 iao:0000111 "protocol"@en,
                        "Protocol"@en;
            iao:0000112 "PMID: 18388943.Nat Protoc. 2008;3(4):612-8.Protocol for the induction of arthritis in C57BL/6 mice."@en;
            iao:0000114 iao:0000122;
            iao:0000115 "a protocol is a plan specification which has sufficient level of detail and quantitative information to communicate it between domain experts, so that different domain experts will reliably be able to independently reproduce the process."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PlanAndPlannedProcess Branch"@en;
            iao:0000119 "OBI branch derived + wikipedia (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protocol_%28natural_sciences%29)"@en;
            iao:0000412 pobo:obi.owl;
            a owl:Class;
            rdfs:label "Protocol";
            rdfs:subClassOf bibo:Document.
obi:0000293 iao:0000111 "has_specified_input";
            iao:0000112 "see is_input_of example_of_usage"@en;
            iao:0000115 "A relation between a planned process and a continuant participating in that process that is not created during  the process. The presence of the continuant during the process is explicitly specified in the plan specification which the process realizes the concretization of."@en;
            iao:0000116 "8/17/09: specified inputs of one process are not necessarily specified inputs of a larger process that it is part of. This is in contrast to how 'has participant' works.";
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Larry Hunter",
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters",
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Melanie Coutot";
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:domain obi:0000011;
            rdfs:label "has specified input";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf pobo:RO_0002233.
obi:0000299 iao:0000111 "has_specified_output";
            iao:0000115 "A relation between a planned process and a continuant participating in that process. The presence of the continuant at the end of the process is explicitly specified in the objective specification which the process realizes the concretization of."@en;
            iao:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot",
                        "PERSON: Bjoern Peters",
                        "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg"@en,
                        "PERSON: Larry Hunter";
            a owl:ObjectProperty;
            rdfs:domain obi:0000011;
            rdfs:label "has specified output";
            rdfs:subPropertyOf pobo:RO_0002234;
            owl:inverseOf obi:0000312.
